[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The reports merged into it
describe more than one problem, and the queued parser fix closes only one of them. Each problem now
has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser does not close #4471. The form hint and the one-day moves stay broken.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- `parser` ([#1](https://github.com/dudziakm/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/1)): the shared parser
  reads every date month first, so a tenant that writes the day first gets day and month swapped.
  "Our 7 April reminder went out on 4 July." It comes in by every channel, from every tenant.
- `hint` ([#2](https://github.com/dudziakm/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/2)): booking-v3's form
  prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, then reads the date day first, the tenant's way. People
  type what the hint says and get the same swap. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants. This form
  reads the date itself, so the parser fix does not reach it.
- `one-day move` ([#3](https://github.com/dudziakm/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/3)): the date
  moves by one day; day and month stay where they are. "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says
  Monday 11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." The desk already read
  these as one-day moves in its notes, but the cause table on #4471 still counts them under `parser`.

## How each report is placed

1. One id, one report: the export repeats reports where its pages overlap.
2. A report the desk read as a one-day move is a `one-day move`.
3. Every other report goes by its tenant, as `causes.ts` does: a form report from a booking-v3
   tenant that writes the day first is `hint`; any other report from a day-first tenant is `parser`.

Intake's tag is not used: it guesses from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant.

## Why one ticket held them all

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match. Most
subject lines come in under more than one problem (the note under the table counts them), so
matching on subjects cannot keep these problems apart. Changing that rule needs a new decision record; 0001
stays as accepted.

## While the desk keeps merging

The table reads the ticket export and the desk notes at render time. A report merged into #4471
later, or one more one-day move in the desk notes, changes the counts on this page without an edit.
The counts in the tickets are from the export of 4 October.

